### Option B: Mundlak Device (Recommended)

The Mundlak (1978) device adds the **within-unit means** of all time-varying regressors to the RE specification. The RE–FE choice becomes a test of whether these group means are jointly zero — a linear restriction that pools straightforwardly under Rubin's rules. The joint test below uses the **D2 statistic** of Li, Meng, Raghunathan & Rubin (1991), which pools the $M$ per-imputation Wald chi-squared statistics into a single $F$ reference distribution.

::: {.panel-tabset}

#### R


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# Compute group means within each imputed dataset and add to the data.
# Group means of time-varying continuous covariates capture the "between"
# variation that distinguishes FE from RE.
add_group_means <- function(d) {
  d |>
    group_by(IDORIGIN) |>
    mutate(
      m_DEMOC3   = mean(DEMOC3,   na.rm = TRUE),
      m_PCGTHOU  = mean(PCGTHOU,  na.rm = TRUE),
      m_PERCHPOP = mean(PERCHPOP, na.rm = TRUE)
    ) |>
    ungroup()
}

a_mundlak <- a.out
a_mundlak$imputations <- lapply(a.out$imputations, add_group_means)

# RE model augmented with group means — the Mundlak (1978) specification
mundlak_formula <- AINEW ~ AILAG + DEMOC3 + MIL2 + LEFT + BRIT +
                   CWARCOW + IWARCOW2 + PCGTHOU + PERCHPOP +
                   m_DEMOC3 + m_PCGTHOU + m_PERCHPOP

res_mundlak <- pool_plm(
  amelia_out = a_mundlak,
  formula    = mundlak_formula,
  index      = c("IDORIGIN", "YEAR"),
  model      = "random"
)

res_mundlak |>
  select(term, estimate, std.error, statistic, df, p.value) |>
  mutate(
    role = if_else(str_starts(term, "m_"), "Mundlak term (between-unit)", "Structural")
  ) |>
  gt(groupname_col = "role") |>
  tab_header(
    title    = "Mundlak (1978) RE model — MI Pooled (M = 20)",
    subtitle = "H₀: group-mean coefficients = 0 ↔ RE is consistent"
  ) |>
  fmt_number(columns = c(estimate, std.error, statistic, p.value), decimals = 4) |>
  fmt_number(columns = df, decimals = 1) |>
  tab_style(
    style     = cell_fill(color = "#fef9c3"),
    locations = cells_body(rows = p.value < 0.05)
  ) |>
  tab_footnote(
    footnote  = "Mundlak terms are the within-country means of each time-varying covariate. Significant terms indicate that between-unit variation drives the coefficient, favouring FE.",
    locations = cells_row_groups(groups = "Mundlak term (between-unit)")
  )
```

